From 632a6bbdcaa1cba4a5af786ac33b2068bab61f91 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michael Knopke <knopkem@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 27 Jul 2026 14:21:58 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/9] Editor: Import scenes on multiple threads

Allow ResourceImporterScene to be imported on worker threads by
overriding can_import_threaded(), and parallelize mesh processing
within a single scene import:

- ResourceImporterScene::import() is made thread-aware: IO errors are
  marshalled to the main thread, scene previews are deferred to
  import_threaded_end(), and post-import scripts/plugins are
  serialized with a mutex (user code is not expected to be
  thread-safe).
- _generate_meshes() is restructured into collect/process/replace
  passes; unique meshes are processed in parallel (LODs, shadow
  meshes, lightmap UV unwrap, index optimization), while tree
  mutation stays serial. When already on a worker thread, meshes are
  processed inline to avoid nested group waits starving the pool.
- EditorProgress task names include the source file so concurrent
  imports don't collide.
- reimport_append() skips node signals and file system tree updates
  when called from an import thread (glTF reimports its extracted
  textures this way).
- The main thread now services synchronous rendering server calls
  from import threads (RenderingServer::sync()) instead of
  busy-waiting on a semaphore, which would otherwise deadlock scene
  packing.
- Dependencies of reimported files are only reimported when they
  actually need it, using cached modification times and destination
  file existence checks.
